 let accepted=read(format!("{Z}/docs/benchmarks/2026-10-30-joint-top-bounded175/artifacts/accepted-rows.json"));save(Path::new(D).join("artifacts/accepted-rows.json"),&accepted);let review=json!({"capture_pins_match":true,"production_files_unchanged":175,"private_original_field_files_recover":17,"native_new_tests":2,"native_exact_lazy_lane_inputs":139184,"inherited_unchanged_field_tests":33,"processes":1732,"latency_processes":latency,"total_kernel_calls_including_primes":total_calls,"component_gate":a["component_gate"],"diagnostics_qualified":q,"SDK_eligible":false,"proof_ledger":25231,"commands":rec,"archives":{"source":src,"helpers":helper,"receipts":receipts_archive,"observations":observations}});save(Path::new(D).join("artifacts/review.json"),&review);
 let mut text=String::from("# Subtracting coordinates before radix splitting\n\n");text+=&format!("The fixed component gate **{}**. Production remains unchanged. This compares packing and arithmetic components, not complete G1/G2 additions, queries or proofs. [Review](artifacts/review.json).\n\n",if a["component_gate"]==true{"passes; separate actual-caller qualification is required"}else{"fails; no actual-caller or SDK integration follows"});text+="The private constructor transposes canonical R256 operands into four saturated64-bit word vectors, computes the exact lazy value p+a-b with carry/borrow masks, then splits only the result to radix52. The original computes two radix52 conversions followed by subtraction. Both produce identical raw lazy limbs. Norm performs two differences and their fused sum of squares; anchors retains both original converted operands for delta*a+b. The latter checks the cost when later curve work still needs the anchors. All field multiplication/reduction bodies remain original. No table, persistent allocation, key-point copy, new plan, scheduler or representation change is added. The constructor is not used by production.\n\n";
 text+="The [DoT paper](https://arxiv.org/html/2604.21566v3), sections3.1–3.2, separates word computation and carry handling. It addresses limbs within a SIMD integer; this prototype keeps eight independent fields and changes where input subtraction occurs. No external speedup is transferred. Earlier parallel normalization, mask-carry and direct-reference packing trials retain their original failed gates. This is a new input dataflow rather than a rerun of those kernels.\n\n";
 text+="## Fixed measurements\n\nRyzen9950X,16physical/32logical CPUs. Solo pins CPU2, physical16 CPUs0–15, logical32 CPUs0–31. Thirty-one fixed rotated/reversed blocks compare frozen original, fresh ordinary and new constructor. Every worker uses independent32 rows of changing full-width inputs, three1024-update checked primes, then32768 updates. Each row cycles deterministically; results accumulate and are checked outside timing against scalar-field sums. The same fresh executable contains both operations with dispatch before the loop. Original and new noinline pattern kernels remain in separate emitted bodies. There is zero allocation in every measured wave; wave latency includes all workers completing. These component inputs are synthetic raw canonical fields, not captured curve coordinates or whole proof workloads.\n\n|Field / pattern / workers|Frozen ns|OFF ns|New ns|Paired New/OFF [bounds]|Wins/31|\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---|---:|\n";
 for(key,m)in a["summaries_ns_per_wave"].as_object().unwrap(){let v=&a["paired"][format!("{key}/new/off")];text+=&format!("|{key}|{:.3}|{:.3}|{:.3}|{:.9} [{:.9}, {:.9}]|{}|\n",m["frozen"].as_f64().unwrap(),m["off"].as_f64().unwrap(),m["new"].as_f64().unwrap(),v["median"].as_f64().unwrap(),v["lower"].as_f64().unwrap(),v["upper"].as_f64().unwrap(),v["wins"]);}
 text+="\nFq32 three-pattern equal-log aggregate, and norm32/anchors32 individually, require upper paired ratios<1 and at least21/31wins versus both controls. Every cell's new/control upper ratio must be<=1.03; all fresh/frozen calibration intervals must fit factor1.03. Ranks10–22/31 have nominal97.055%individual coverage conditional on independent exchangeable blocks, without a familywise guarantee. No gain floor, exclusions, extension, changed thresholds, successful reruns or favorable-subset promotion. [Every paired comparison and failed check](artifacts/analysis.json).\n\n";
