 text+="## Correctness, source and diagnostics\n\nTwo new native field tests pass139184 exact lazy-lane inputs over both primes, covering raw powers/modulus boundaries and deterministic random operands. An independent u128/overflowing-sub word oracle checks exact p+a-b, then canonical results and following products match original arithmetic. The33 unchanged field tests are inherited, not rerun. No actual curve/prover integration or portable qualification is claimed. All175 production hashes remain exact; removing one include recovers all17 private field originals. The accepted raw word transpose is copied byte-exactly. The new private API assumes canonical inputs below p and only supports R256. [Bounds](artifacts/bounds.md), [source](artifacts/field-source.json.gz).\n\nThe initial offline dependency resolution requested an unavailable cached libc version; the original manifest is retained and only its pin changed to cached0.2.191. The first new-test compilation stopped before executing any test because its extracted transpose needed an explicit unsafe block and the test array needed an explicit length. Original sources/plans/pins/failed receipts and the two syntax/type repairs are retained. Frozen successful build is reused. No arithmetic or performance protocol changed after a successful test; no successful test/build/capture repeats.\n\n";
 text+=&format!("All{} successful workflow commands complete, including54preflights,1674latency processes,four separate profiles and16postcapture commands. All1732processes match scalar output oracles and cross-variant digests; total{} component updates including primes. No SDK request or Gnark proof is generated.\n\n",rec["successful_commands"],total_calls);
 text+="Profiles follow all latency: fixed16M cycles:u,4194304updates per worker, FIFO enabled after primes and disabled before output checking. All recordings finish before ownership changes, decoding, hashes and archive work. Every helper is compiled/pinned before capture, with no overlapping owned build/helper/hash/archive/analyzer or other benchmark. Per-worker TID/CPU, time, mappings, fixed-period and loss metadata remain in exact receipts.\n\n|Profile|Samples|Unknown period fraction|All workers sampled|Qualified|\n|---|---:|---:|---|---|\n";
